# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true at the SYSTEM level, so on a
# Windows checkout git rewrites every LF it believes belongs to a text file into
# CRLF. Several of the playground's assets are not text: they are LENGTH-FRAMED
# binary containers whose headers carry an exact <bytelen>. Injecting one CR into
# such a file desynchronises every frame after it, the reader's walk stops dead,
# and the playground silently loses its entire pre-semchecked std surface — the
# default program then reports "undeclared routine `echo`" with nothing wrong in
# the code. Marking them binary is what stops that from ever happening again.
#
# Later rules win, so the catch-all comes FIRST and the binary overrides follow.

# Text: normalise to LF in the repository, and check it out as LF too. The
# toolchain, the content hashes and the shell scripts all assume LF.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Not text. `binary` == `-text -diff`: never translate, never diff as text.
*.bin           binary
*.nif           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.wasm          binary
*.zip           binary
